msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1497
msgid "CrowdSec is a free, open source security engine whose users share the IPs that attack them. Its community blocklist holds scanners, brute-forcers and scrapers seen on many sites, residential proxies among them, which the limits of a single site cannot recognise in time. With your own CrowdSec agent (on a VPS: install CrowdSec, then run “cscli bouncers add scrapelock” for the key), ScrapeLock asks it every 15 minutes for what changed. Without one, use the address of a CrowdSec Console blocklist integration (key: user:password) or of another plain-text list; it is downloaded once an hour. Private addresses, ranges wider than /16 (IPv6 /32), this server, CDN edges and official search engine addresses are never taken from a list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1502
msgid "Address of the CrowdSec agent (LAPI) or of the list:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1506
