msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1506
msgid "Kept in the database and never shown or exported. To keep it out of the database, define SCRAPELOCK_CROWDSEC_KEY in wp-config.php instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1507
msgid "What a listed IP gets:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1513
msgid "A 403 on every request"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1515
msgid "Addresses change hands (mobile networks, home connections that get a new address every day, VPNs), so a list is never certain. The stricter limit lets a real visitor read on slowly; the 403 refuses outright. A listed IP earns no violation either way."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1518
msgid "Pages per minute for listed IPs (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1523
msgid "Block after this many violations within 10 minutes (0 = never):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1523
msgid "Violation: every minute in which the IP exceeded a limit, and every fake Googlebot. The trap blocks immediately: for 10 minutes the first time, for the full time if the same IP falls into it again within 24 hours."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1524
