#: includes/class-pncp-origin.php:211
msgid "Requests reach WordPress from a reverse proxy or load balancer on this server or a private network (REMOTE_ADDR is 127.0.0.1, the server's own address or a private address such as 10.x or 172.16-31.x, with a forwarding header such as X-Forwarded-For), but “Real visitor IP” does not read the visitor's address from it. Every visitor then has the proxy's address: on 127.0.0.1 they all pass as the server itself and are not checked, and on a private address nothing is limited or banned per IP (a ban would block the whole site). On the Bots tab, set “Real visitor IP” to the header the proxy sets (usually X-Forwarded-For or X-Real-IP); a proxy on the server or a private network is trusted for it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-origin.php:257
msgid "Requests reach WordPress from a reverse proxy on this server (REMOTE_ADDR is 127.0.0.1 or the server's own address, with a forwarding header such as X-Forwarded-For), but that proxy is not trusted. ScrapeLock cannot tell them from the server's own requests, so “Only through the CDN” lets them all through, also the ones that went around the CDN. On the Bots tab, set “Real visitor IP” to the header the proxy sets (usually X-Forwarded-For or X-Real-IP); a proxy on the server itself is trusted for it."
msgstr ""

